video_component = '<article class="ds-panel ds-component" id="feed-video"><h3>Video playback</h3><div class="ds-card-layout"><div class="ds-card-specimen">' + video_card + '</div><div class="ds-component-spec"><h4>Uploaded video loop</h4><p>Trending Videos uses four different user-supplied clips: a city content walk, an LED skincare lounge, meal prep and a laundry reset. Each preview links to its own fictional Trend Detail article, whose main video uses the same tall 9:16 portrait frame as the city content-walk article. The original 16:9 files are preserved and cropped with object-fit: cover inside that frame. Visible previews autoplay muted. Tapping the video body pauses or resumes playback with the existing transient play/pause feedback. A primary Go deeper link opens the matching article, while the 48px sound control restores or mutes its original audio. Reduced-motion preferences start playback paused. Only one preview plays at a time. Offscreen pausing and keyboard support are shared with the article players. The 9:16 video cards use --radius-md (10px) corners and clip their media. The second editorial feed story now uses the supplied still photograph and links to its article.</p><p>The retailtainment article uses the supplied still photo as its main image. All four Go Deeper articles—city content walk, LED skincare lounge, Sunday meal prep and weekly laundry reset—use the shared tall 9:16 article video frame with muted autoplay, tap to pause/play, sound control, offscreen pausing and reduced-motion behavior. Each plays its matching clip above the article text; the LED article uses the video instead of its former still image. Every article video uses the carousel’s 24px volume symbol (--icon-size-lg) within a 48px target. The symbol box sits 24px from the bottom (--spacing-layout-lg) and 12px from the right (--spacing-component-ms); target positioning accounts for its extra space. These insets apply on desktop and mobile.</p><p><a class="ds-text-link" href="../feed.html#feed-video-story">Open the still-image feed story</a> · <a class="ds-text-link" href="../trend-city-content-walk.html">Open the article video</a></p></div></div></article>'
